    "problem_statement": "### Issue with Async Client Authentication\n\nDescription\n\nIt seems there's an issue with the authentication process in the asynchronous client. After applying the recent changes, the client is not handling the credentials correctly, which leads to unexpected behavior when performing certain actions.\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n\n1. Initialize the `AsyncBaseClient` with valid credentials.\n2. Attempt to perform actions such as following/unfollowing a user or list, liking/unliking a tweet, or managing pinned lists.\n3. Observe that these actions fail to execute as expected.\n\nExample:\n\n```python\nfrom tweepy.asynchronous import AsyncBaseClient\n\nclient = AsyncBaseClient(\n    bearer_token=\"your_bearer_token\",\n    consumer_key=\"your_consumer_key\",\n    consumer_secret=\"your_consumer_secret\",\n    access_token=\"your_access_token\",\n    access_token_secret=\"your_access_token_secret\"\n)\n\n# Attempt to follow a user\nawait client.follow_user(user_id=\"123456789\")\n```\n\nExpected Result:\n- The user should be followed successfully.\n\nActual Result:\n- The operation fails, and the user is not followed.\n\nThis issue seems to affect multiple functionalities related to user interactions and timeline management. It would be great to have this looked into to ensure the client handles authentication and actions correctly."
  }
